  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>During boiling&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is converted to insoluble&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Boiling</mi></mover><mi>Mg</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8595;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>boiling</mi></mover><msub><mi>CaCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8595;</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;changes to insoluble&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Mg(OH)<sub>2​</sub>&nbsp;is less soluble than&nbsp;MgCO<sub>3.&nbsp;</sub>Hence, the products formed are CaCO<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;and Mg(OH)<sub>2</sub>.​</p>",
